<%# THE DOOR (Shop manual slice 8; the `sign-in` screen): every signed-out Devise page in one frame.
    The left half names the product and shows one of the app's own renders; the right half holds the
    page's own boxes, which each caller passes as the block. Rendered with `render layout:` so the
    sign-in, sign-up, first-run, password and confirmation pages cannot drift apart.

    STILL THE PLAIN CARD OF design-system.md rule 15, not the landing: one sentence, one lead and
    one figure, no wall, no features and no demo pitch. The demo's door stays the sign-in page's own
    box, and only while Tinkerex::Demo.available? (users/sessions/new).

    `.auth-card` IS THE WHOLE DOOR NOW, both halves: every test that pins the card's brand, form,
    links and primary asks for a descendant of it, and those all still hold (rule 12: restyle, never
    rename). The brand is a <div>, not a link: a signed-out visitor has no Home to go to.

    THE FIGURE IS THE LANDING WALL'S RENDER OF hex tiles.lbrn2 (Tinkerex::Landing::TILES; written by
    `bin/rails landing:wall` from db/seeds/demo, never drawn or edited), on the ink-on-paper card
    every render sits on (rule 5). It carries a figure number because the door is drawn as a page of
    a manual; it is a mark, which rule 13 lets the accent draw. %>
<div class="auth-card">
  <div class="auth-intro">
    <div class="brand"><span class="brand-mark" aria-hidden="true"></span><span class="brand-name">Tinkerex</span></div>
    <p class="auth-slogan">The manual for everything you make.</p>
    <p class="auth-lead">Your files, your projects and your stock, kept on your own server and shown at
      their real size.</p>
    <figure class="auth-figure">
      <span class="thumb">
        <%= image_tag "landing/wall/hex-tiles-lbrn2.png", width: Tinkerex::Landing::SIZE, height: Tinkerex::Landing::SIZE,
                      alt: "A sheet of hexagonal game tiles drawn for the laser, each engraved with its own pattern" %>
        <span class="fig-num" aria-hidden="true">1</span>
      </span>
      <figcaption>
        <span class="auth-figure-label">Fig. 1</span>
        <span>Hex tiles for a board game.</span>
        <span class="auth-figure-file">hex tiles.lbrn2</span>
      </figcaption>
    </figure>
  </div>
  <div class="auth-forms">
    <%= yield %>
  </div>
</div>
